resolution={
 'shared':'n is sample size, d the covariate dimension and N the number of random features. Bold W has shape N by d, its rows are w_l, and bold theta is an N-vector. The data-model signal bold beta is a d-vector. Standard primitives include Gaussian laws, sphere-uniform laws, Euclidean norms, inner products, matrix transpose, positive-semidefinite square root, Hadamard product, finite sums, expected loss, min/max/supremum and convergence in probability. A2 supplies the N-dimensional all-ones vector, A4 the matrix norm and indicator conventions. No library availability is asserted.',
 '4.2':'D1-D7 resolve all nonlocal objects. Tau squared is the noise marginal variance in (2.1), psi1 and psi2 come from Assumption 1, epsilon is the positive training radius and epsilon_test the separate test radius. Scalar sigma squared, the five saddle variables, their starred solution, the objective R and its lambda supremum are bound/defined inside the theorem. The ordinary error function erf is used without a main-text definition; its conventional real definition is 2/sqrt(pi) times the integral of exp(-t^2) from 0 to its argument. The root nu-star and the subscripted nu_star in the final formula are not silently identified; see source note. The limiting probability is expressly over both training data and W. Proof-only J, Gaussian surrogates, the event E_W, zeta penalties and constraint sets C_theta are not statement dependencies.',
 '6.9':'D1/D2/D3 supply data, W and the shifted activation. D8 is the explicitly assumed event E_W, D9 supplies J, and D11 supplies sample surrogate features f_i with coefficients D10. D12 supplies the reiterated dimensional limit convention. Phi_A and Phi_B are inline definitions, theta ranges over the N-dimensional coefficient space, lambda/lambda_s/lambda_w are inline positive parameters, bold1 is A2, and c is the common proposed limit. The theorem compares optimum values, not minimizers or risks. Its adjacent Proposition 6.10 and constraint set C_theta-prime are not imported as hypotheses.'
}
def main():
    (ROOT/'ambient-conventions.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(paper_id=PID,auxiliary_passages=aux,standard_ambient_resolution=resolution,unresolved_source_conventions=issues),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
    print('Saved',len(aux),'auxiliary passages and',len(issues),'source notes.')


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
